    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35540" root="قرظ" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظِىٌّ</span></b>  The <i>dye</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِبْغ</span> [a mistranscription for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبْع</span> i. e. <i>tan</i>]) <i>of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْرُوظٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ قَرَظِيَّةٌ</span> <i>Camels that eat</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظ</span>. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كبش قَرَظِىٌّ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُرَظِىٌّ</span> <i>A ram of El-Yemen;</i>
because the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَظ</span> grows there [most plentifully].
(S, K.)

